#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Simulation capabilities allow you to test your robot's software in virtual "
"environments, often with physical accuracy. This article summarizes ROS "
"developer tools and guidance available to enable simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Area: simulation, capabilities | Content-type: about | Experience: "
"beginner, intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:24
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:27
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:29
msgid ""
"It's not always feasible to build, train, and test robotic applications in "
"their real-world environments. Simulation capabilities support development "
"by making it possible to use the same ROS software in virtual environments "
"that accurately represent the physical world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:32
msgid "ROS capabilities are enabled by community-contributed packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:35
msgid "Community-contributed packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:37
msgid ""
"`Gazebo <https://docs.ros.org/en/lyrical/Tutorials/Advanced/Simulators/"
"Gazebo/Simulation-Gazebo.html>`_: A toolbox of development libraries and "
"cloud services for simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:39
msgid ""
"`Webots <https://docs.ros.org/en/lyrical/Tutorials/Advanced/Simulators/"
"Webots/Simulation-Webots.html>`_: A robotics simulator for modeling, "
"programming, and testing robots in a realistic 3D physics environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:41
msgid ""
"`Isaac Sim <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacSim>`_: A cloud-based "
"simulation platform for developing and testing robotic applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Simulation.rst:43
msgid ""
"`O3DE <https://github.com/o3de/o3de>`_: An open-source, cross-platform 3D "
"game engine for creating immersive experiences."
msgstr ""
